- op: discuss  # 15e5
  at: '2026-06-17T15:18:07Z'  # 15e5
  by: agent  # 15e5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 15e5
  clock: 3  # 15e5
  nonce: '15e5'  # 15e5
  message: "Core defects fixed & merged (selfh/dev 826d5296e7, via auto-pr). (1) SWALLOW: the reverse-slice ran as a bare command under 'set -euo pipefail', so a non-zero slice exit aborted the script BEFORE SLICE_EXIT was captured and before the run_full_suite fallback could run -> opaque exit-1, no log, zero tests. Fixed with the '|| SLICE_EXIT=$?' capture idiom so the existing fallback is reachable. BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: forcing a slice failure (HG_PATH=/bin/false bash scripts/smart-test --manifest) now exits 0 with the fallback firing (manifest 'Mode: full-suite / Reason: slice command failed', diagnostic written to .ci/smart-test-fallback.log), vs the prior empty exit-1 (the two backgrounded runs + the timeout-90 trace that showed it stuck in 'hypergumbo slice'). (2) FAILOVER BASELINE: get_baseline anchored merge-base on stale origin/dev; now failover-aware (selfh/dev under .git/CI_FAILOVER_ACTIVE, guarded on the ref resolving). EVIDENCE: baseline moved from stale 613bda8b (206 changed files) to current selfh/dev (3 changed files). Static guard tests pin both properties (packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_smart_test_slice_robustness.py, 3/3). DEFERRED to follow-up WI-<see next>: the last-green-sha WRITE side is dead end-to-end -- .github/workflows/full-suite.yml writes the marker only inside an exact-100%-coverage branch that currently never fires, so both remotes' badges branches carry only coverage.json. The read side is corrected here so the optimization activates for free once the write side lands."  # 15e5
